{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 11: The Attention Mechanism",
  "description": "See how attention lets every token look at every other token!\n\nTHIS IS WHAT MAKES TRANSFORMERS SPECIAL:\nInstead of processing tokens one-by-one (like LSTM),\nattention lets all tokens communicate SIMULTANEOUSLY.\n\nTHE KEY INSIGHT:\nEach token asks: \"Who should I pay attention to?\"\n- Query (Q): What am I looking for?\n- Key (K): What do I contain?\n- Value (V): What information do I carry?\n\nTRY THIS:\n1. Select different input tokens\n2. Watch how attention weights change\n3. See which tokens attend to which!\n\nThis is the foundation of GPT, Claude, and every modern AI.",
  "metadata": {
    "created": "2025-12-19T22:00:00",
    "modified": "2025-12-19T22:00:00",
