    {
      "id": "comment-tutorial",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "name": "Tutorial Explanation",
      "position": [
        1064,
        406
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": " THE ATTENTION MECHANISM - How Transformers Think!\n\nThis is the breakthrough that powers GPT, Claude, and every\nmodern AI. Let's see how it works!\n\nTHE FLOW:\n1. TOKEN INPUTS: Three words forming a mini-sequence\n   Try: 'the', 'cat', 'it' - watch what 'it' attends to!\n\n2. EMBEDDINGS: Each word becomes a 16D vector\n   Similar words have similar vectors\n\n3. POSITIONAL ENCODING: Adds position info\n   Without this, 'cat ate fish' = 'fish ate cat'!\n\n4. SELF-ATTENTION (the magic):\n   - Q: What am I looking for?\n   - K: What do I contain?\n   - V: What info do I carry?\n   \n   Each token computes: 'Who should I attend to?'\n   Score = Q dot K (high = relevant)\n   Output = weighted sum of V (blend relevant info)\n\n5. ATTENTION WEIGHTS HEATMAP:\n   Bright = high attention!\n   Watch how 'it' attends to 'cat' - pronoun resolution!\n\nTHE BIG INSIGHT:\nLSTM processes tokens ONE BY ONE (sequential)\nAttention sees ALL tokens AT ONCE (parallel)\n\nThis is why transformers are so powerful and fast!\n\nTRY THIS:\n- Change 'it' to different tokens\n- Watch attention patterns shift\n- This is literally how AI understands language!",
        "width": 450,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Tutorial explanation"
    }
  ],
